{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And they charged — unto Joseph.</b> Like ״וַיְצַוֵּם אֶל בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל״ — He charged Moses and Aaron to be emissaries unto the children of Israel; so too here, וַיְצַוּוּ אֶל — they charged their emissary, to be an emissary unto Joseph to say thus to him. And whom did they charge? The sons of Bilhah, for they were regulars with him, as it is said: ״וְהוּא נַעַר אֶת בְּנֵי בִלְהָה״." "<b>Your father charged.</b> They altered the matter for the sake of peace, for Jacob had not so charged — Joseph was not suspect in his eyes (Bereshit Rabbah; Yevamot 65)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 50, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:04:28.416397764Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}